<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-303007-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-303007-1')">1</a>. It's debateable as to why we want to preserve the spirit of bad articles as opposed to opening a slot for something with the primary quality of being <em>good</em>, but that's a separate discussion</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-303007-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-303007-2')">2</a>. Standard disclaimer that this doesn't mean I want to see more GoI references of any sort goes here.</div>
