			<div class="content" id="post-content-2370012">
									

<p>My major problems have largely been stated by others. Finding out that it always produces things that cause children to injure adults, well, that's just boring. I actually found the compulsion effect more interesting, although 1) that might have just been in contrast to the rest of the content and 2) such a huge statistical margin is overkill. Takes it from a potential slight nudge into a big consciousness-altering shove.</p>
<p>For more technical issues, I don't understand why you included the section on cards and chalk, given that you do not even remotely use them for the rest of the article. It confuses the description having extra items and special rules for them before the items that actually have any effect, and smacks strongly of &quot;it's there because it was in the original.&quot;</p>
<p>-1</p>

